## Code quality

- **ruff** for linting and formatting
- **ty** for type checking
- **pytest** for testing with coverage

Run `just check` before committing.

## Continuous integration

[% if not ci_enabled %]
**The workflows are off in this repository**: they run only when started
by hand (`gh workflow run ci.yml`), since private repositories pay for
GitHub Actions minutes beyond a free monthly quota. Run `just check` and
`just test` locally before every pull request. Switch them on with
`uvx copier update --trust --data ci_enabled=true`.

[% endif %]
Every pull request and every push to `main` runs one workflow on GitHub
Actions, **CI**, which sums up its checks in one check, `ci-ok`. A pull
request that changes only docs skips the type check and the platform
tests (`tools/ci_changes.py` says which files are docs). CI runs:

- **Python Code Quality:** checks that `uv.lock` is up to date, runs ruff
  (lint and format) and ty (types), and checks the paths named in
  `AGENTS.md` files and skills.
- **Platform Tests:** the test suite on Linux, Windows, and macOS. The Linux
  job uploads the coverage to Coveralls and posts it as a comment on the
  pull request.
- **Docs Quality:** a language check (Vale) of the changed pages, and a
  link check (lychee) of the built site. Pull requests check the links
  between our pages only; the weekly run also checks the external links
  and opens an issue when one fails.

## Releasing

Releases are cut by a maintainer, never by a coding agent. A release is the
git tag `[[ dist_name ]]-v<version>` on `main` and a GitHub release; nothing
is published to PyPI or Zenodo from this repository
([How a release works](releasing.md)).

```bash
just versions                                     # current version
just changelog                                    # changes since the last release
git checkout -b chore/release-[[ dist_name ]]-0.2.0
just release [[ dist_name ]] minor                # or major, patch, or e.g. 0.2.0
git push --no-follow-tags -u origin chore/release-[[ dist_name ]]-0.2.0
gh pr create --fill
# once merged:
git checkout main && git pull
just tag                                          # tags main and pushes the tag
```

`just release` runs the package's tests and makes one commit that sets the
version in `packages/[[ dist_name ]]/pyproject.toml` (and `uv.lock`) and
writes `packages/[[ dist_name ]]/CHANGELOG.md` from the commits
([git-cliff](https://git-cliff.org), `cliff.toml`). A minor or major release
also gets a release notebook, `release-notes/[[ dist_name ]]-v<version>.py`,
copied from `release-notes/_template.py` and committed on the release
branch. Pushing the tag drafts a GitHub release from the changelog
(`release.yml`); publish it by hand.
